=== WHY THE TEST WAS WRONG, AND WHAT CHANGED ===
P18.6's MOLAR route (reactionHeatRelease) needs only q and Delta H_r, so it accepts any
finite q -- it deliberately does NOT duplicate P18.4's direction validation. The MASS route
goes through reactionSpeciesSources, which DOES validate. So a negative q is representable
in one route and refused in the other, for a reaction declared Irreversible.

That asymmetry is correct: validating direction in two places would be a duplicated
invariant. The TEST was wrong to compare the two routes at a rate only one of them accepts.

FIX: the negative-rate comparison moves to a REVERSIBLE reaction, where a net negative rate
is legitimate and both routes accept it. The irreversible cases keep q >= 0.
NO THRESHOLD CHANGED and no guard was weakened.
